An embedded core board, often implemented as a System on Module (SoM), integrates computing components such as a processor or system-on-chip, memory, storage and power-management functions. Depending on its design, a module may also support wireless connectivity, graphics or AI acceleration. It can be incorporated into a carrier board designed for the specific interfaces and functions of the finished product.

